        "title": "Future Architectures: Neuromorphic, Quantum, Accelerators",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Post-Moore's law computing explores architectures that do not rely on transistor scaling for performance gains. The major directions: (1) specialization — custom silicon for specific workloads; (2) integration — CXL, chiplets, memory-near-compute; (3) neuromorphic — event-driven spiking neural networks; (4) quantum — superposition and entanglement for specific algorithms."
